# OctoFit Tracker Frontend Configuration

## Codespaces Environment Setup

For GitHub Codespaces, set the following environment variable in `.env.local`:

```bash
VITE_CODESPACE_NAME=your-codespace-name
```

### Example .env.local

```
# Replace with your actual Codespace name
# You can find it in the Codespace URL: https://your-codespace-name-xxx.github.dev
VITE_CODESPACE_NAME=my-octofit-app

# The frontend will automatically construct the API URL as:
# https://${VITE_CODESPACE_NAME}-8000.app.github.dev
```

### Fallback to Localhost

If `VITE_CODESPACE_NAME` is not set or is undefined, the application will automatically fall back to:
```
http://localhost:8000
```

This allows for seamless development in both local and Codespaces environments.

## API Endpoints

The application connects to the following API endpoints:

- `/api/users/` - User management
- `/api/teams/` - Team management
- `/api/activities/` - Activity logging
- `/api/leaderboard/` - Competitive rankings
- `/api/workouts/` - Workout recommendations

## Starting the Application

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

The application will start on `http://localhost:5173`

## Building for Production

```bash
npm run build
npm run preview
```
